A map read in Kotlin falls back to the value type's zero, `m[k] ?: zero`, as
a key the map lacks reads on every other target. A struct had no zero there
but `null`, so the Pokédex's `(facts[m] ?: null).kind` did not compile; a
struct the program declares is a data class with a default for every field,
and its zero is that class called with none.

deny out/kotlin/android/app/src/main/java/test/sngl/app/MainScreen.kt `\?: null\)` -- a struct's zero is a value of it

-- m.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

struct Fact {
    kind  string
    power option[int]
}

component moves ui.node {
    var facts map[string, Fact] = {}

    ui.button(text="Learn", @click { facts["tackle"] = Fact{kind="normal", power=40} })
    ui.text(value=facts["tackle"].kind)
}

ui.window {
    moves()
}
